==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|mezzen}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*metaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmɛsn̩/|/ˈmɛsən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-messen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=5|misst|maß|gemessen|past subjunctive=mäße}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[measure]] (something)
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[compete]]
#: ''sich mit jemandem '''messen''''' — “to compete with someone”
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[measure]]; to be a given size, height, width, length, etc.
#: {{ux|de|Der Tisch '''misst''' 160 Zentimeter.|The table measures 160 centimeters.}}

